decisions:
  - id: D-conductor-global-install
    decision: 'Three-tier binary resolution: ~/.paradigm/conductor/bin/ → monorepo dev → error'
    rationale: Simplest path to global access. No Homebrew tap, no npm binary package, just file copy. User runs --install once from monorepo, then works everywhere.
  - id: D-conductor-resume-terminal
    decision: Resume opens interactive terminal, not headless agent. Claude auto-recovers via MCP.
    rationale: User wants to be at the helm — interactive sessions, not background agents. paradigm_session_recover already runs on session start, so no special injection needed.
  - id: D-conductor-linking-groups
    decision: Instance linking creates AgentGroupStore groups with Symphony agent IDs
    rationale: All infrastructure exists (AgentGroupStore, NoteRelay, AgentPartManager). UI is just checkboxes + group creation. Real-time message passing requires /conduct registration, which is a known next step.
learnings:
  - 90% of the daily-driver gap was binary distribution and data population, not missing features
  - SessionManagerView already had full project cards with checkpoint context — just needed better button labels and a data source
  - ProjectStore was empty because nothing ever called addOrUpdate — auto-discovery from _project-meta.json files solved it in 30 lines of Swift
  - Instance linking backend was fully built across 3 services (AgentGroupStore, AgentPartManager, NoteRelay) — only the selection UI was missing
