body: |-
  ## What Changed

  Conductor has been a fully-featured macOS overlay app for 20 sprints — voice input, gaze tracking, gesture recognition, window tiling, Symphony integration, Sentinel live view, task dashboard, agent health monitoring. But it could only launch from inside the a-paradigm monorepo because `findConductorDir()` walked up from `__dirname` looking for `Package.swift`.

  This session closed 4 gaps:

  ### 1. Global Binary Install
  `paradigm conductor --install` builds the Swift binary and copies it to `~/.paradigm/conductor/bin/conductor` (11.5MB, arm64). The launch command now checks there first, then falls back to monorepo dev binary, then errors with install instructions. Works from any directory.

  ### 2. Auto-Discover Projects
  `CheckpointReader.discoverAllProjects()` scans `~/.paradigm/sessions/*/` and reads `_project-meta.json` from each. `ProjectStore.discoverAndMerge()` runs on init, populating the project list with ~22 projects immediately. Filters out projects whose paths no longer exist on disk.

  ### 3. Resume UX
  Renamed buttons: "Resume" (with checkpoint, primary) → opens Terminal.app in project dir. "Open" (no checkpoint) → same. "Headless" → secondary, for power users who want background agents. The key insight: `paradigm_session_recover` runs automatically via MCP, so just opening a terminal in the right directory is sufficient for context recovery.

  ### 4. Instance Linking
  Link icon in Sessions header toggles linking mode. Select 2+ projects → "Link" creates an AgentGroup via AgentGroupStore with Symphony agent IDs. The group persists to `~/.paradigm/conductor/groups.json`. Backend infrastructure (NoteRelay, AgentPartManager, SymphonyMonitor) is fully built — linking is the last-mile UI.

  ## What's Still Rough

  - Terminal sessions need `/conduct` registration for Conductor to see them as live instances
  - No auto-update for installed binary — need `--install` again after monorepo rebuild
  - Instance linking creates groups but real-time Symphony messaging requires both sessions to have registered agent parts
  - Project list shows all historical projects, no search/filter yet

  ## Next: Brand Identity & Layout Overhaul

  User wants:
  - Sidebar (collapsible) + composable NxM grid for terminal cells
  - In-app help system (? button with docs on capabilities, menus, what's rough)
  - Full brand facelift across Conductor, Platform, Sentinel, Lore, University
  - This is the beginning of a larger design initiative
